  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "Final rules are strict on reporting (24h all incidents, 48h customer notice) and require 55°C testing with a 5% threshold but allow corrective action instead of automatic sales stop, with customer disclosure but no public per-model rates. Remote shut-off is required immediately for new units and within 6 years for installed units with a feasibility escape; built-in fire suppression is required at 36 months. Recall is mandatory above 8/100k with 48h urgent notices, but no serious-injury clause or transition phase."
